---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="About JSON Lens" description="Why JSON Lens is a focused, browser-first JSON formatter, validator, and inspector.">
  <main id="main-content" class="site-main site-shell" tabindex="-1">
    <header class="page-intro"><div><p class="eyebrow">About</p><h1>Small tool, clear behavior.</h1></div><div class="page-intro__aside"><p class="page-intro__lede">JSON Lens is built around a simple idea: when a payload is hard to read, the tool should show what it found and keep the input close to you.</p></div></header>
    <section class="section"><div class="section-head"><div><p class="eyebrow">What we optimize for</p><h2>Trust is a feature.</h2></div><p>Formatting, validation, safe repair, comparison, tree inspection, copying, and downloading run in the browser. The interface names its behavior, avoids invented performance claims, and links to the research behind the product decision.</p></div><div class="tool-note"><p><strong>Current scope:</strong> strict JSON formatting, minification, line-aware errors, reversible repair, structural comparison, document statistics, file input, and searchable structure.</p><p><strong>Product boundary:</strong> one focused workflow. Additions must make JSON easier to understand without turning the page into a generic utility directory.</p></div></section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
